<!--
# Dynamic Scripting - a sandboxed script acting on the live world

`<DynamicComponent>` mints a component type with no rust definition behind it,
and `<DynamicScript>` runs a sandboxed script with a `world` API installed.
Every `world` method is served the moment it is awaited, so a script reads what
it just wrote, a `spawn` hands back a real entity id the next line can use, and
a refused call is an error the script can catch.

The muster script spawns the squad and reads one of them straight back, so the
world it describes is the world it just made. The round script uses real ids
throughout, and the last beat asks for something its exposure forbids, catches
the refusal and writes it onto the roll call, whose `<Log::Name>` reports it.

    beet --main=examples/action/dynamic_script.bsx
-->
<Fragment>
	<!-- the vocabulary this document mints, kept by the scene rather than
	expanded away, so it survives a serde round trip. The schema is what the
	word means: every write to it is validated before it lands -->
	<DynamicComponent name="game.Health" schema="u64"/>
	<Sequence {CallOnReady}>
		<DynamicScript
			{ScriptExposure{read:["bevy_ecs::name::Name","game.Health"],write:["bevy_ecs::name::Name","game.Health"]}}
			script="
			// muster: each fighter is spawned with a registered rust component,
			// addressed by its full type path, beside the minted one
			await world.spawn({ 'bevy_ecs::name::Name': 'ada', 'game.Health': 3 });
			await world.spawn({ 'bevy_ecs::name::Name': 'bob', 'game.Health': 5 });
			const cleo = await world.spawn({ 'bevy_ecs::name::Name': 'cleo', 'game.Health': 2 });

			// the spawn resolved to a real entity, so it can be read back at once
			const health = await world.get(cleo, 'game.Health');
			console.log('cleo mustered with ' + health + ' health');
			"/>
		<DynamicScript
			{ScriptExposure{read:["bevy_ecs::name::Name","game.Health"],write:["bevy_ecs::name::Name","game.Health"]}}
			script="
			// the roll call is named but carries no health, so it is no fighter
			let report = null;
			for (const id of await world.entities('bevy_ecs::name::Name')) {
				if ((await world.get(id, 'bevy_ecs::name::Name')) === 'roll call') {
					report = id;
				}
			}

			// the round: everyone takes a hit and the weakest is renamed. Each
			// read is of the world as it is now, so the roster is what landed.
			const roster = [];
			let weakest = null;
			for (const id of await world.entities('game.Health')) {
				await world.insert(id, 'game.Health', (await world.get(id, 'game.Health')) - 1);
				const name = await world.get(id, 'bevy_ecs::name::Name');
				const health = await world.get(id, 'game.Health');
				roster.push(name + ' ' + health);
				if (weakest === null || health <= weakest.health) {
					weakest = { id, health, name };
				}
			}
			await world.insert(weakest.id, 'bevy_ecs::name::Name', weakest.name + ' (wounded)');
			await world.insert(report, 'bevy_ecs::name::Name', 'roll call ' + roster.join(', '));
			"/>
		<DynamicScript
			{ScriptExposure{read:["bevy_ecs::name::Name","game.Health"],write:["game.Health"]}}
			script="
			// this script may read a name but not write one, and the refusal
			// arrives as an error where the call was made
			const [named] = await world.entities('bevy_ecs::name::Name');
			try {
				await world.insert(named, 'bevy_ecs::name::Name', 'silenced');
			} catch (err) {
				console.log('refused: ' + err.message);
			}
			"/>
		<Log::Name {Name("roll call")}/>
	</Sequence>
</Fragment>
